From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:36:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: apple_z2: Keep the J71b interrupt masked until the
 controller is woken

On a wake from sleep the controller boots in the background while the
screen is already lit, so the first taps arrive during the boot. The
interrupt was enabled before the 2.26 s pause that precedes the wake
command, and every touch in that window was read early: each data phase
answered with another header ("header in the data phase"), and once
the wake command followed, the controller stopped interrupting for good
(its reply e1 56 00 eb 02 00 eb 01 ..., the same as earlier stall
captures). Touch then stayed dead until the next sleep and wake, with
nothing in the log. Reproduced on the J71b by tapping right after a
10 s sleep.

Enable the interrupt only after the wake command and the report setup.
The level interrupt holds the queued touches in the controller until
then; they are read as soon as the boot finishes, about 3.3 s after
resume. A boot nobody touches is unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c | 16 ++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
index 161ebb4b85be..eaec6e3b7994 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
@@ -3776,10 +3776,6 @@ static int apple_z2_upload_firmware(struct apple_z2 *z2)
 		error = apple_z2_gen1_drain(z2);
 	if (!error && apple_z2_is_j71b(z2))
 		error = apple_z2_gen1_set_level_irq(z2);
-	if (!error && apple_z2_is_j71b(z2) && z2->upload_irq_masked) {
-		z2->upload_irq_masked = false;
-		apple_z2_irq_on(z2);
-	}
 	mutex_unlock(&z2->io_lock);
 	if (error)
 		return error;
@@ -3787,9 +3783,21 @@ static int apple_z2_upload_firmware(struct apple_z2 *z2)
 	if (!apple_z2_uses_ipad_protocol(z2))
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * J71b: the interrupt stays masked until the controller has been
+	 * woken. Touches before that are not delivered as frames: every data
+	 * phase answers with another header, and after the wake the
+	 * controller stopped interrupting for good. On a wake from sleep the
+	 * screen is lit while this runs, so the first taps come here. With
+	 * the level interrupt masked they wait in the controller instead.
+	 */
 	msleep(2260);
 	mutex_lock(&z2->io_lock);
 	error = apple_z2_j172_init_writes_locked(z2);
+	if (!error && apple_z2_is_j71b(z2) && z2->upload_irq_masked) {
+		z2->upload_irq_masked = false;
+		apple_z2_irq_on(z2);
+	}
 	mutex_unlock(&z2->io_lock);
 	return error;
 }
